All 17 tests pass. Here's what I implemented:

**`transpose.py`** — a `transpose(text)` function that:
1. Splits input text into lines (rows of a matrix)
2. Iterates column-by-column (0 to max line length)
3. For each column, collects characters from each row, padding with spaces when a row is too short but a later row still has content at that column
4. Truncates trailing empty padding (no right-padding)

This handles all the edge cases: ragged lines, preserved trailing spaces in columns, and left-padding with spaces.
